{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the general antiderivative of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e1960c50e381dd510e29b913d59dd14c213043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = e^{x}\\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65cea2771427b9c132d4e1200b0477722d75a34c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -e^{x}\\sin x + C \\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ e^{x}\\sin x + C \\quad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{e^{x}}{2}(\\sin x - \\cos x) + C \\quad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{e^{x}}{2}(\\sin x + \\cos x) + C \\quad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{e^{x}}{2}(\\cos x - \\sin x) + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"947\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use integration by parts with the DI method by differentiating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> and integrating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13a313c9231ccaa699c1929a7126a313f1adbda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />. Both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13a313c9231ccaa699c1929a7126a313f1adbda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> are cyclical when integrating or taking the derivative, suggesting that we can choose either of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13a313c9231ccaa699c1929a7126a313f1adbda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> to differentiate or integrate and that we continue until the integral expression repeats. For convenience, we choose to differentiate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> and integrate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13a313c9231ccaa699c1929a7126a313f1adbda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b93f7ce984c3f5e06e36e677af14934cac910e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import fontsize;  size(7cm); defaultpen(fontsize(12pt));  string[][] data = { \t{&quot;&quot;, &quot;$D$&quot;, &quot;$I$&quot;}, \t{&quot;$+$&quot;, &quot;$\\cos x$&quot;, &quot;$e^x$&quot;}, \t{&quot;$-$&quot;, &quot;$-\\sin x$&quot;, &quot;$e^x$&quot;}, \t{&quot;$+$&quot;, &quot;$-\\cos x$&quot;, &quot;$e^x$&quot;} };  real[] cw = {0.3, 0.6, 0.6};   // column widths real rh = 0.3;                     // row height (adjust to taste)  real[] xb = {0}; for(int j = 0; j &lt; cw.length; ++j) xb.push(xb[j] + cw[j]);  int R = data.length; int C = data[0].length;  pen grid = black + linewidth(0.8); pen lightRed= rgb(&quot;FFCCCB&quot;);  // Horizontal lines for(int i = 1; i &lt;= R - 1; ++i) draw((0, -i*rh)--(xb[C], -i*rh), grid);  // Vertical lines for(int j = 1; j &lt;= C - 1; ++j) draw((xb[j], 0)--(xb[j], -R*rh), grid);  // Cell contents for(int i = 0; i &lt; R; ++i) for(int j = 0; j &lt; C; ++j) label(data[i][j], ((xb[j] + xb[j+1])/2, -(i + 0.5)*rh), align=Center);  draw(((xb[0] + xb[0+1])/2, -(1 + 0.5)*rh)--((xb[1] + xb[1+1])/2, -(1 + 0.5)*rh)--((xb[2] + xb[2+1])/2, -(2 + 0.5)*rh), lightRed+linewidth(14bp)+opacity(0.15));  draw(((xb[0] + xb[0+1])/2, -(2 + 0.5)*rh)--((xb[1] + xb[1+1])/2, -(2 + 0.5)*rh)--((xb[2] + xb[2+1])/2, -(3 + 0.5)*rh), lightRed+linewidth(14bp)+opacity(0.15));  draw(((xb[0] + xb[0+1])/2, -(3 + 0.5)*rh)--((xb[2] + xb[2+1])/2, -(3 + 0.5)*rh), lightRed+linewidth(14bp)+opacity(0.15)); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"265\" />\nWe stop at the third row after seeing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13a313c9231ccaa699c1929a7126a313f1adbda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> in the same row. We therefore have\n\\begin{align*}\n\t\\int e^{x}\\cos x \\, dx &amp;= e^{x} \\cos x + e^{x} \\sin x - \\int e^{x}\\cos x \\, dx\\\\\n\t2 \\int e^{x}\\cos x \\, dx &amp;= e^{x} \\cos x + e^{x} \\sin x\\\\\n\t\\int e^{x}\\cos x \\, dx &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{e^{x}}{2}(\\sin x + \\cos x) + C}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 28 (page does not exist)\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School C